----Feature suggestions that can be converted into Github issues
[]Apply validation (via the setter) on DiscreteRadiation.source
[]unitfy the process for loading default data/coefs, storing data/coefs, and then re-loading the stored coefs/data, for {efficiency,resolution,peak_to_compton} curves.
    - See the following table for details of how it's currently done:
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    |           Quantity            |      Resolution & count rate          | Efficiency                        | Compton-to-peak ratio             |
    --------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    |Class (callable?)              | ResolutionMaxCountRate (no)           | EfficiencyCurve (yes)             | ComptonToPeakRatioCurve (yes)     |
    |Support Class (callable?)      |                                       |                                   | PeakToComptonCoefficients (no)    |

    |How the default data is stored | Outputted as magic values by          | Raw datapoint file, referenced by | Raw datapoint file, referenced by |
    |(& How to point to file path)  | get_default_resolution_coefficients() | physicalparameters/filepaths.py   | physicalparameters/filepaths.py   |
    |                               | (no default for count rate)           |                                   |                                   |

    |How to load the default data   | resolution_curve_factory(             | EfficiencyCurve.from_file(        | ComptonToPeakRatioCurve.from_file(|
    |                               |get_default_resolution_coefficients()  |get_default_efficiency_curve_path()|get_default_peak_to_Compton_file() |
    |                               | )                                     | )                                 | )                                 |

    |How to load custom data        | ResolutionMaxCountRate(               | EfficiencyCurve.from_file() ONLY  | ComptonToPeakRatioCurve(floats) OR|
    |                               | fit_fwhms(), max_count_rate )         |                                   |ComptonToPeakRatioCurve.from_file()|

    |How to save the coefficients/  | ResolutionMaxCountRate.save()         | desired: EfficiencyCurve.save()   | ComptonToPeakRatioCurve.save()    |
    |data used for this run         |                                       | current: save_as_efficiency_file()|                                   |

    |How to reload the saved data   | ResolutionMaxCountRate.load()         | desired: EfficiencyCurve.load()   | desired:                          |
    |                               |                                       |                                   |   ComptonToPeakRatioCurve.load()  |
    |                               |                                       | current: find_efficiency_file()   | current: ComptonToPeakRatioCurve( |
    |                               |                                       |                                   |   PeakToComptonCoefficients.load()|
    |                               |                                       |                                   | )                                 |
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    - resolution (default stored in python file) -> stored in plain .txt file -> re-load from coefs
    - efficiency (default stored as .csv file) -> copied as data with various file endings -> re-load from data
    - peak-to-Compton (default stored as .csv file) -> coefficients stored in .txt file -> re-load from coefs
    If possible, follow the API used by the Compton-to-peak ratio column
